      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T21:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mm... but I\u0027d have to pass host_cmd_handler_args. It seems weird to be making decisions about which command version is supported and which response version form to send back so deep in the feature code. Given that this is not a hot command, I\u0027d prefer to have the versioning/command-form stuff out here, since the overhead is minimal and it reduces the chances of messing things up in the future if this these parameters are adopted by others or this command is extended again.\n\nBut you\u0027re right, I should just just pass ec_params_host_sleep_event_v1 and ec_response_host_event_sleep_v1 down into power_chipset_handle_host_sleep_event(), so that I\u0027m not juggling all these different fields. I will do that.",
